<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="061" project="spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI">
  <metadata>
    <title>Credential census test — source analysis, not DI resolution (FR-F2)</title>
    <phase>6 Forcing Functions</phase>
    <gate>022 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies tests/**; TEST-MODIFYING override makes code-review + adr-check unconditional.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Structural test with a clear specification.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>G</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>022</deps>
    <tags>testing,auth,archtest,forcing-function</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Assert that the number of confidential-client construction sites equals a checked-in census, each entry carrying a reason. Adding a ninth site must fail until the census is updated. This is what would have caught SpeAdminTokenProvider and SpeAdminGraphService, both absent from the origin seed's inventory.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with NetArchTest experience.</role>
  <goal>A checked-in credential census enforced by a test, so an unlisted confidential client cannot appear silently.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>The origin seed counted 5 confidential-client sites; the real number was 8. The two it missed were per-customer SpeAdmin paths. A census makes the count itself the assertion, so the next miss is a build failure rather than a discovery two projects later.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/CredentialCensusTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/CREDENTIAL-INVENTORY.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/GodClassGuardTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies><dependency task="022" status="pending">The end-state site list</dependency></dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: MUST be source or assembly analysis. A census implemented as Assert.NotNull(services.GetRequiredService&lt;X&gt;()) is a BANNED DI-registration test (ban B3) and would become the anti-pattern this task exists to prevent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the census enumerates ConfidentialClientApplicationBuilder construction sites and their credential source, each with a one-line reason.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: seed the census from CREDENTIAL-INVENTORY §1 — 8 sites — adjusted for the Phase 2 migration end state.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: include the maintenance procedure in the test comment, matching the sibling ratchet tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>NetArchTest, credential inventory</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>tests/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/CREDENTIAL-INVENTORY.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Enumerate confidential-client construction sites by source or assembly analysis.</step>
    <step>Write the census with per-site reasons, seeded from the inventory.</step>
    <step>Assert count equality; fail with a diff naming the unlisted site.</step>
    <step>Add a negative control proving the detector fires on a seeded new site.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Source analysis cannot reliably enumerate construction sites (e.g. they are built via a factory indirection) — report; a census that undercounts is worse than none because it creates false confidence.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="new">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/CredentialCensusTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Adding a ninth confidential-client site FAILS the build until the census is updated.</criterion>
    <criterion>The failure message names the unlisted site.</criterion>
    <criterion>Every census entry carries a one-line reason.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: the test performs NO DI container resolution — verified by inspection against ADR-038 ban B3.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative control proves the detector fires.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
